==Battleground==
*1 [[Kory]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Oldhorn]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*1 [[Kory]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Oldhorn]] spawns after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Berserkory]] spawns after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The biggest threats in this stage are not the Oldhorns, but rather the Kories and the Berserkories. Their presence in the stage along with the Oldhorn essentially requires the usage of [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]], as not using meatshields will allow the Oldhorns to push extremely quickly. Focus on killing the Kories first, then once the first Oldhorn spawns, use him as a stepping stone to stack as many [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] units as possible on it. Once the Oldhorn dies, your DPS stack should be able to kill the second Kory in no time. Rinse and repeat for the second Oldhorn. By the time Berserkory comes out, the second Oldhorn should be dead. You will want to spam as many wave shields as possible during this phase, and your DPS stack will eventually kill this Berserkory. After this, you should be able to beat the stage. If not, and the final Berserkory comes out, rinse and repeat.

